1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,940
For almost seventy years he lay in a nameless grave behind a church wall,

2
00:00:03,960 --> 00:00:07,150
and in the end he was identified by a small metal tag.

3
00:00:07,200 --> 00:00:08,790
His name was Kurt Knispel.

4
00:00:08,810 --> 00:00:10,800
He was a Wehrmacht tank soldier,

5
00:00:10,820 --> 00:00:13,030
first a loader, then a gunner,

6
00:00:13,110 --> 00:00:17,350
and finally commander of a Tiger in Heavy Panzer Battalion 503.

7
00:00:17,370 --> 00:00:21,720
With it he fought on the Eastern Front, in 1943 also at Kursk.

8
00:00:21,770 --> 00:00:26,270
Many books credit him with 168 destroyed tanks,

9
00:00:26,290 --> 00:00:31,560
supposedly 126 as a gunner and 42 as a commander.

10
00:00:31,600 --> 00:00:33,870
That number cannot be confirmed,

11
00:00:33,890 --> 00:00:37,600
because his battalion did not count kills for individual crews.

12
00:00:37,620 --> 00:00:41,690
Historians also consider some of the stories about him embellished.

13
00:00:41,710 --> 00:00:46,500
What is certain is that in 1944 he received the German Cross in Gold.

14
00:00:46,520 --> 00:00:51,280
He never received the Knight's Cross and never rose above the rank of sergeant.

15
00:00:51,300 --> 00:00:55,740
Reportedly he was seen as difficult and openly contradicted his superiors,

16
00:00:55,760 --> 00:00:59,280
and wore his hair and beard longer than regulations allowed.

17
00:00:59,320 --> 00:01:06,230
In late April 1945, days before the end of the war, his King Tiger was hit in South Moravia.

18
00:01:06,250 --> 00:01:09,940
According to his radio operator, a shell splinter wounded him in the head.

19
00:01:09,960 --> 00:01:14,460
Knispel died in a field hospital in the village of Urbau, today Vrbovec.

20
00:01:14,480 --> 00:01:16,330
After that, all trace of him was lost.

21
00:01:16,380 --> 00:01:21,430
Only in 2013 did archaeologists find a grave there with sixteen German soldiers.

22
00:01:21,450 --> 00:01:24,150
His identity tag lay with one of them.

23
00:01:24,210 --> 00:01:31,250
In November 2014 the German War Graves Commission reburied him in the military cemetery in Brno,

24
00:01:31,270 --> 00:01:34,530
among fallen soldiers whose names hardly anyone still knows.
